## 2025-02-17 - Added aria-hidden to decorative Material Symbols and explicit label bindings
**Learning:** Google Material Symbols implemented as text ligatures in `<span>` tags (e.g., `<span class="material-symbols-outlined">gavel</span>`) will be read aloud by screen readers as the ligature text ("gavel") unless explicitly silenced. In complex forms, implicit label associations (wrapping the input, or relying on visual proximity in a flex layout) are insufficient; explicit `for` and `id` mappings (plus `aria-describedby` for helper text) are required for robust screen reader navigation.
**Action:** Always add `aria-hidden="true"` to purely decorative icon fonts/ligatures. Always verify that form controls have explicit `<label for="...">` attributes and utilize `aria-describedby` when supplementary hint text is provided near the input.
